WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.862 --> 00:00:09.723
and John were hiking in a forest.

2
00:00:13.887 --> 00:00:16.689
"We have been friends for many years," Tomas said.

3
00:00:16.709 --> 00:00:19.031
"Yes, we have."

4
00:00:19.832 --> 00:00:20.793
John smiled.

5
00:00:20.813 --> 00:00:24.016
"Ever since we were children!"

6
00:00:29.484 --> 00:00:31.906
Tomas was lucky because he had made a fortune.

7
00:00:33.186 --> 00:00:34.627
Now he lived in a mansion.

8
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:41.412
Meanwhile John was poor and lived in a small cabin.

9
00:00:41.432 --> 00:00:46.615
"I think your family needs a new house," Tomas said.

10
00:00:46.635 --> 00:00:52.980
"Of course we do, but we are too poor," John said.

11
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.264
"Please let me help you build a new house," Tomas said.

12
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.941
"I've had good luck, and I want to share it."

13
00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:05.164
"Thank you, Tomas," John said.

14
00:01:05.184 --> 00:01:07.646
"That sounds wonderful.

15
00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:09.427
You're a true friend!"

16
00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:12.770
The friends continued hiking.

17
00:01:16.052 --> 00:01:18.634
As they climbed up a hill, they spotted a bear.

18
00:01:20.936 --> 00:01:23.458
The bear growled and began running toward them.

19
00:01:24.859 --> 00:01:25.759
John was a fast runner.

20
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.721
Leaving Tomas behind, he ran as fast as he could.

21
00:01:34.321 --> 00:01:35.682
He raced up a tall tree.

22
00:01:37.782 --> 00:01:39.303
But Tomas froze in fear.

23
00:01:42.464 --> 00:01:44.624
The bear was coming closer and closer!

24
00:01:44.644 --> 00:01:48.525
"It's no use," Tomas thought.

25
00:01:48.545 --> 00:01:50.286
"This bear will eat me!"

26
00:01:52.386 --> 00:01:54.347
Suddenly Tomas had an idea.

27
00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:57.428
"Bears might not eat dead people," he thought.

28
00:01:59.008 --> 00:02:01.749
So Tomas lay down on the ground and held his breath.

29
00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.310
He tried to lie very still.

30
00:02:09.371 --> 00:02:09.911
don't eat me.

31
00:02:10.411 --> 00:02:12.132
Please!" Tomas thought.

32
00:02:13.052 --> 00:02:14.973
John nervously watched from the tree.

33
00:02:16.193 --> 00:02:19.494
The bear sniffed Tomas, but Tomas did not move.

34
00:02:20.694 --> 00:02:23.915
The bear looked at Tomas closely and then licked his ear.

35
00:02:24.875 --> 00:02:26.516
Tomas still did not move.

36
00:02:27.664 --> 00:02:29.685
At last the bear walked away.

37
00:02:33.526 --> 00:02:35.466
John climbed down and ran to Tomas.

38
00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:40.208
John said.

39
00:02:40.228 --> 00:02:42.248
"We're both safe.

40
00:02:43.248 --> 00:02:44.689
Thank goodness the bear didn't hurt you!"

41
00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.470
Tomas looked away.

42
00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.391
"Right. The bear didn't hurt me," he said coldly.

43
00:02:53.611 --> 00:02:55.972
John was surprised by his friend's cold tone.

44
00:02:56.672 --> 00:02:57.713
"You should be happy, Tomas.

45
00:02:58.313 --> 00:02:58.993
You're alive!"

46
00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:00.854
Tomas shrugged.

47
00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:02.074
"I guess so."

48
00:03:02.094 --> 00:03:05.056
"Huh?" John thought.

49
00:03:05.076 --> 00:03:07.257
"Why is Tomas so upset?"

50
00:03:07.277 --> 00:03:09.718
"Were you scared, Tomas?

51
00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:12.179
I saw the bear lick your ear.

52
00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.380
You probably thought it was about to eat you!"

53
00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.741
Tomas frowned.

54
00:03:16.761 --> 00:03:18.521
"Yes, John.

55
00:03:18.781 --> 00:03:19.842
The bear licked my ear.

56
00:03:20.902 --> 00:03:22.383
But it also whispered something.

57
00:03:23.443 --> 00:03:24.744
It said, 'Your friend ran away.

58
00:03:26.036 --> 00:03:28.899
A true friend always stays nearby and helps.'"

59
00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.061
John was stunned.

60
00:03:33.784 --> 00:03:37.467
As Tomas walked away alone, John felt sad and ashamed.

61
00:03:38.828 --> 00:03:40.250
He had thought only of himself.

62
00:03:41.451 --> 00:03:43.373
Now he had lost his friend forever.

63
00:03:45.895 --> 00:03:50.419
As the bear said, a true friend always stays nearby and helps.
